<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mieszko II the Fat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1220–1246</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-ii-lambert">Mieszko II</a> the Fat (c. 1220–1246) was a Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-opole">Casimir I of Opole</a>. During the Mongol invasion of 1241 he fought the raiders near Racibórz and then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious">Henry II the Pious</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnica">Battle of Legnica</a>, from which his force withdrew. He died without children, and his lands passed to his brother Władysław.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mieszko-ii-the-fat.jpg" alt="Mieszko II the Fat" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous plate · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mieszko_II_Oty%C5%82y_seal_1245.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
